===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|rootbeer}}

===Etymology===
First recorded in 1841. {{rfe|en}}

===Pronunciation===
{{IPA|en|/ˈɹut ˌbɪɹ/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A beverage, most often a [[carbonated]] [[soft drink]] made from a combination of [[vanilla]], [[cherry]] tree [[bark]], [[licorice]] root, [[sarsaparilla]] root, [[sassafras]] root bark, [[nutmeg]], [[anise]]{{,}} and [[molasses]], among other things.
#: {{cot|en|root tea}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2002|author=Todd Wilbur|title=Top Secret Recipes|publisher=Penguin|isbn=9781101118672
|passage=In 1919, when Roy Allen and Frank Wright started selling their new '''root beer''' beverage to a thirsty America, national Prohibition was taking its grip on the country. Their timing couldn't have been better. No longer able to legally drink real beer, thirsty patriots had to settle for this sweet, foamy conoction derived from roots, herbs, and berries.}}
# {{lb|en|color}} A dark [[reddish]]-[[brown]] color, like the drink.
#: {{color panel|root beer|6B3232}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2000|author=w:Mark Z. Danielewski|title=w:House of Leaves|page=26
|passage=I just keep staring at all the ink we have, that wild variety of color, everything from '''rootbeer''', midnight blue and cochineal to mauve, light doe, lilac, south sea green, maize, even pelican black, all line up in these plastic caps{{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006|author=Tim Lewis|title=Bows, Swamps, Whitetails|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=89rKrOcTc9oC&pg=PA28&dq=%22root+beer+shade%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=166eVbfFCcjToATm_7WgBg&ved=0CCYQ6AEwAA|page=28
|passage={{...}}most of our bucks have antlers that are varying degrees of brown, from a deep rich '''root beer''' shade to walnut to even light amber.}}

